1
00:00:12,738 --> 00:00:15,938
(Jung Yong Hwa)

2
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:19,038
(Hong Seung Hee)

3
00:00:19,108 --> 00:00:22,308
(Lee Yi Kyung)

4
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:25,278
(Park Yu Na)

5
00:00:36,628 --> 00:00:40,028
(Oh! My Guard)

6
00:00:40,098 --> 00:00:41,528
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

7
00:00:41,598 --> 00:00:43,038
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:45,738 --> 00:00:48,008
There are two kinds of men in this world.

9
00:00:48,368 --> 00:00:51,778
Men who need a bodyguard, and men who don't.

10
00:00:51,838 --> 00:00:53,178
(Han Jung Woo, Director at BS Group, Group Heir)

11
00:00:53,248 --> 00:00:54,448
(Under threat from his half-siblings)

12
00:00:55,448 --> 00:00:59,148
If a handsome, gentlemanly man loved by everyone...

13
00:00:59,218 --> 00:01:00,788
happens to be the heir to this conglomerate,

14
00:01:01,348 --> 00:01:02,988
it does not matter which kind he is.

15
00:01:03,758 --> 00:01:04,758
But...

16
00:01:06,888 --> 00:01:10,158
If he is under threat from half-siblings pushed aside,

17
00:01:10,998 --> 00:01:12,398
that changes everything.

18
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:14,768
Hey, Han Jung Woo. Pull over. You better stop!

19
00:01:14,828 --> 00:01:16,068
Hey, I said pull over!

20
00:02:13,828 --> 00:02:14,828
Floor it!

21
00:02:21,628 --> 00:02:22,628
What's going on?

22
00:02:24,068 --> 00:02:25,438
- What is happening?
- Open the door!

23
00:02:25,438 --> 00:02:26,468
- Grab him.
- Darn it.

24
00:02:26,468 --> 00:02:27,508
Let's out!

25
00:02:41,988 --> 00:02:43,018
What?

26
00:02:46,528 --> 00:02:47,528
Who is that?

27
00:03:39,338 --> 00:03:40,608
(Cha Hong Du, Taekwondo Master, Part-Time Queen)

28
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:42,448
(The toughest woman in the neighbourhood)

29
00:03:43,448 --> 00:03:44,948
You were a woman?

30
00:03:45,018 --> 00:03:46,948
Of course, I am a woman.

31
00:03:47,348 --> 00:03:50,118
A bold, tough woman who can fight.

32
00:03:53,328 --> 00:03:55,328
I guess I don't need to work out today.

33
00:03:56,828 --> 00:03:58,598
Darn it. I'm going to be so late.

34
00:04:02,168 --> 00:04:03,168
Hey, wait.

35
00:04:04,968 --> 00:04:08,008
You can't just leave like that. At least tell me your name.

36
00:04:09,068 --> 00:04:10,078
Hong Du.

37
00:04:11,038 --> 00:04:12,038
Cha Hong Du.

38
00:04:13,708 --> 00:04:15,448
Cha Hong Du?

39
00:04:31,058 --> 00:04:34,498
That's how we met, like it was fate...

40
00:04:36,438 --> 00:04:38,198
I wish.

41
00:04:38,338 --> 00:04:41,008
("The Crown Prince's Bodyguard" continues in episode two)

42
00:04:41,138 --> 00:04:44,378
That was the story of the heroine in that drama.

43
00:04:45,438 --> 00:04:46,908
And as for me,

44
00:04:46,978 --> 00:04:51,718
I am a drama nerd who has watched this show over a million times.

45
00:04:52,448 --> 00:04:54,618
And that man in particular...

46
00:04:55,118 --> 00:04:57,418
I am Um Tae Bong's biggest fan.

47
00:04:58,158 --> 00:05:01,058
Watching my favourite drama and losing myself in daydreams...

48
00:05:01,558 --> 00:05:03,258
is my greatest joy in life.

49
00:05:03,258 --> 00:05:04,928
You could call it living vicariously.

50
00:05:05,258 --> 00:05:08,268
Someone I want to be but never can.

51
00:05:09,638 --> 00:05:10,868
Because...

52
00:05:11,598 --> 00:05:14,468
Ms. Hae Ra, your meal is ready.

53
00:05:17,208 --> 00:05:21,148
Have you ever heard of anthropophobia?

54
00:05:21,778 --> 00:05:26,588
Ever since second grade, I have never once stepped outside.

55
00:05:27,388 --> 00:05:30,088
School? Not applicable.

56
00:05:31,018 --> 00:05:33,228
No friends either, you ask?

57
00:05:33,658 --> 00:05:35,228
That goes without saying.

58
00:05:35,828 --> 00:05:39,428
Still, I know what I need to know.

59
00:05:40,168 --> 00:05:44,538
I already know full well how scary the outside world is.

60
00:05:45,268 --> 00:05:49,138
Thanks to the news, I have got ethics and social studies down pat.

61
00:05:50,638 --> 00:05:52,078
A couple set of figurines.

62
00:05:52,138 --> 00:05:53,578
(Lovely couple pigs)

63
00:05:53,648 --> 00:05:55,548
One is mine.

64
00:05:57,048 --> 00:05:58,148
And the other one...

65
00:05:59,218 --> 00:06:00,288
See that?

66
00:06:00,348 --> 00:06:03,118
I am well-versed in spending and economics too.

67
00:06:03,188 --> 00:06:04,418
(The Crown Prince's Bodyguard)

68
00:06:04,488 --> 00:06:05,718
Oh, physical training?

69
00:06:19,098 --> 00:06:21,738
If I were the heroine of that drama,

70
00:06:22,168 --> 00:06:24,238
I could protect him too.

71
00:06:24,838 --> 00:06:26,878
Ms. Hae Ra, what happened?

72
00:06:27,878 --> 00:06:30,448
I am sorry, Mr. Nam Goong.

73
00:06:32,378 --> 00:06:36,248
- It is all right.
- I am a bit uncoordinated.

74
00:06:36,658 --> 00:06:37,688
But still, I...

75
00:06:37,758 --> 00:06:41,728
Napoleon rose from soldier to emperor,

76
00:06:41,788 --> 00:06:44,398
and he left us the famous words, "Nothing is impossible."

77
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:45,758
Thanks to Mr. Nam Goong,

78
00:06:45,828 --> 00:06:49,738
- I am a very cultured recluse.
- Miss,

79
00:06:51,638 --> 00:06:54,508
how about going outside with me today?

80
00:06:56,008 --> 00:06:57,038
Not yet.

81
00:06:57,578 --> 00:07:01,948
Yes, then whenever you want to walk out that door yourself...

82
00:07:06,788 --> 00:07:08,588
I ran into her in the living room earlier,

83
00:07:08,648 --> 00:07:10,418
and she just ran right away.

84
00:07:10,418 --> 00:07:12,558
She eats alone and plays alone.

85
00:07:12,618 --> 00:07:15,458
It is easier to just treat her like a ghost.

86
00:07:15,528 --> 00:07:18,358
A ghost? Oh my, how pitiful.

87
00:07:18,828 --> 00:07:20,728
But why does she eat separately?

88
00:07:20,798 --> 00:07:22,968
How would I know? Mind your own business.

89
00:07:23,398 --> 00:07:26,398
Why should we care about a daughter the Chairman ignores?

90
00:07:52,998 --> 00:07:56,498
Nobody likes me.

91
00:07:58,098 --> 00:08:00,438
What does it feel like...

92
00:08:01,468 --> 00:08:02,908
being loved by someone?

93
00:08:17,958 --> 00:08:20,728
I wish something would happen to me too.

94
00:08:21,258 --> 00:08:23,898
Suddenly, just like that rain.

95
00:08:41,478 --> 00:08:43,618
(Oh! My Guard)

96
00:08:45,418 --> 00:08:47,788
(Episode 1)

97
00:09:02,498 --> 00:09:04,098
Do not come closer. Stop right there.

98
00:09:04,168 --> 00:09:06,838
The two of them kiss. It is written in the script.

99
00:09:06,908 --> 00:09:09,338
Since when did you have such a passion for acting?

100
00:09:09,408 --> 00:09:10,438
You can't even act.

101
00:09:11,838 --> 00:09:12,938
Cut!

102
00:09:13,448 --> 00:09:14,548
What? Who just yelled cut?

103
00:09:14,808 --> 00:09:16,048
Was it me? Was it you?

104
00:09:17,478 --> 00:09:18,478
It was me.

105
00:09:18,748 --> 00:09:20,948
Oh, it was you, Tae Bong.

106
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:23,458
But I am the director, and I did not yell cut.

107
00:09:23,458 --> 00:09:24,988
Man, it was going so well just now.

108
00:09:25,058 --> 00:09:29,058
Exactly. My emotions were perfect just now too.

109
00:09:29,428 --> 00:09:31,358
I thought you were different from the others, Director.

110
00:09:31,358 --> 00:09:32,428
What?

111
00:09:35,268 --> 00:09:37,038
I am completely crazy about this woman.

112
00:09:39,098 --> 00:09:40,638
My eyes were already doing all the work,

113
00:09:40,708 --> 00:09:43,308
and the viewers would be totally immersed with their hearts pounding.

114
00:09:43,378 --> 00:09:46,378
Then the minute-by-minute ratings would obviously hit their peak.

115
00:09:46,948 --> 00:09:47,948
And?

116
00:09:48,008 --> 00:09:51,518
And yet you insist on ending it with the leads locking lips,

117
00:09:51,578 --> 00:09:54,618
believing it is the only way to transmit love to viewers,

118
00:09:54,688 --> 00:09:58,558
the illogical and uncreative style of Korean dramas...

119
00:09:59,618 --> 00:10:02,688
You are not that kind of lousy director, are you?

120
00:10:03,528 --> 00:10:06,398
Oh, well, I am not on the lousy side. Gosh...

121
00:10:08,028 --> 00:10:11,298
No, but it is a romance, so if we leave out the kiss scene...

122
00:10:11,368 --> 00:10:14,408
The ratings will drop, and we will lose advertisements.

123
00:10:14,468 --> 00:10:16,408
- Exactly.
- Want to make a bet?

124
00:10:17,638 --> 00:10:18,678
Darn it.

125
00:10:19,738 --> 00:10:21,678
Hey, this is the ending scene for episode eight.

126
00:10:21,678 --> 00:10:23,448
The ending of episode eight has to be a kiss.

127
00:10:23,518 --> 00:10:24,648
We've trained them to expect it,

128
00:10:24,718 --> 00:10:26,548
so how can we change the viewers overnight?

129
00:10:26,618 --> 00:10:30,018
I know you don't shoot kiss scenes. I know.

130
00:10:30,088 --> 00:10:32,288
But just this once, do it as a favour to me.

131
00:10:35,988 --> 00:10:38,658
Then, as a favour to you, Director...

132
00:10:40,198 --> 00:10:43,298
I will not shoot it. Absolutely no kiss scenes.

133
00:10:43,368 --> 00:10:44,468
(The Cocky Detective and Con Artist, Filming in progress)

134
00:10:44,538 --> 00:10:46,398
Why? Why on earth not?

135
00:10:46,468 --> 00:10:48,868
Why would you refuse to shoot something so good?

136
00:10:48,938 --> 00:10:50,638
- Because I don't want to.
- Shoot it.

137
00:10:51,178 --> 00:10:53,308
- I will not.
- Shoot it.

138
00:10:53,508 --> 00:10:56,008
- I absolutely will not.
- Hey, Um Tae Bong!

139
00:10:59,178 --> 00:11:00,188
Just as I thought.

140
00:11:02,848 --> 00:11:03,988
You are lousy.

141
00:11:05,688 --> 00:11:07,488
"Lousy?" Hey, you punk!

142
00:11:07,988 --> 00:11:11,398
The word I hate the most is lousy! Seriously!

143
00:11:11,498 --> 00:11:12,658
Oh, darn it.

144
00:11:13,258 --> 00:11:15,528
Call the writer. Tell her I could not persuade that jerk.

145
00:11:15,598 --> 00:11:16,838
This is driving me crazy.

146
00:11:16,898 --> 00:11:21,138
I mean, what kind of romance master refuses to shoot kiss scenes?

147
00:11:21,208 --> 00:11:23,508
And who made him that romance master?

148
00:11:23,578 --> 00:11:25,538
I'm Pyo Jin Gosh!

149
00:11:25,608 --> 00:11:29,148
But he wants to attach a label like "does not shoot kiss scenes" to it?

150
00:11:29,208 --> 00:11:32,148
That is exactly why he is crazy.

151
00:11:32,218 --> 00:11:34,718
If he were next to me, I would have beaten him to death.

152
00:11:34,788 --> 00:11:36,418
This is already his third project with me.

153
00:11:36,488 --> 00:11:39,218
If he keeps refusing this time, I will make his character...

154
00:11:40,128 --> 00:11:41,858
into complete trash!

155
00:11:43,058 --> 00:11:45,128
I will be sure to pass that on to the trash.

156
00:11:51,668 --> 00:11:52,698
I passed it on.

157
00:11:55,008 --> 00:11:56,838
I heard you had a fight with the director too.

158
00:11:56,908 --> 00:11:58,678
Why did you talk down to the director?

159
00:11:58,738 --> 00:12:00,978
Should I drop my age next time?

160
00:12:02,008 --> 00:12:03,008
Or my forehead?

161
00:12:04,848 --> 00:12:06,278
Oh, I ought to just...

162
00:12:07,948 --> 00:12:10,788
A romantic comedy lead refusing to shoot a kiss scene.

163
00:12:11,788 --> 00:12:14,328
Where do I even begin to study this rare specimen?

164
00:12:14,388 --> 00:12:15,428
Do not study me.

165
00:12:15,488 --> 00:12:19,358
You have made a lot of money off this rare item so far, CEO Park.

166
00:12:19,428 --> 00:12:20,968
Are you in the mood for jokes right now?

167
00:12:21,028 --> 00:12:23,268
There is going to be another scandal now!

168
00:12:25,598 --> 00:12:26,598
Gosh.

169
00:12:28,308 --> 00:12:30,438
Oh, I need to hold it in.

170
00:12:30,508 --> 00:12:32,978
Should we have just revealed everything from the very beginning?

171
00:12:33,548 --> 00:12:34,578
No.

172
00:12:34,648 --> 00:12:37,148
If we did, would you have blown up like this out of nowhere?

173
00:12:37,948 --> 00:12:40,918
But you still have those romantic eyes,

174
00:12:40,988 --> 00:12:43,618
- so let us keep pushing forward.
- What if we reveal it...

175
00:12:44,158 --> 00:12:45,158
even now?

176
00:12:46,218 --> 00:12:47,858
The reason why I don't shoot kiss scenes.

177
00:12:48,558 --> 00:12:51,398
You got famous from romance, and romance is where you sell best.

178
00:12:51,458 --> 00:12:54,268
Your life as a romance actor would be dead.

179
00:12:54,328 --> 00:12:55,498
And that is...

180
00:12:56,968 --> 00:12:58,838
a fatal flaw as a man, too.

181
00:13:00,438 --> 00:13:02,208
What are you looking at, punk? Darn you.

182
00:13:04,878 --> 00:13:05,908
What?

183
00:13:06,478 --> 00:13:07,478
A flaw?

184
00:13:09,978 --> 00:13:13,248
Let's set up a dating rumour first. It worked last time, too.

185
00:13:13,448 --> 00:13:15,288
You are the only one in Korea...

186
00:13:15,348 --> 00:13:16,488
whose dating rumours boost your popularity.

187
00:13:16,548 --> 00:13:20,258
Just stick with the sexy and decadent playboy image.

188
00:13:20,388 --> 00:13:22,128
A win-win strategy with women...

189
00:13:22,188 --> 00:13:23,928
who want to get famous through you, just like now.

190
00:13:24,998 --> 00:13:26,198
Tae Bong,

191
00:13:26,628 --> 00:13:27,828
you trust me, right?

192
00:13:27,868 --> 00:13:29,028
I will be the only one...

193
00:13:30,198 --> 00:13:32,068
who knows your secret until the day I die.

194
00:13:32,868 --> 00:13:34,168
Look hard for one.

195
00:13:36,108 --> 00:13:37,308
I am going to the interview.

196
00:13:37,378 --> 00:13:38,508
Oh, okay.

197
00:13:39,308 --> 00:13:40,308
Have a good time.

198
00:13:43,278 --> 00:13:44,948
(CEO Park Hwan Su)

199
00:13:46,748 --> 00:13:50,188
Where am I going to find a girl who is naive...

200
00:13:50,618 --> 00:13:52,558
but can keep a secret this time?

201
00:13:59,328 --> 00:14:00,728
- I'll do it.
- Okay.

202
00:14:02,298 --> 00:14:03,638
Shall we begin?

203
00:14:04,038 --> 00:14:05,138
Yes.

204
00:14:05,498 --> 00:14:08,508
After the unprecedented hit "The Crown Prince's Bodyguard,"

205
00:14:08,568 --> 00:14:10,278
this is your first reunion in three years.

206
00:14:10,338 --> 00:14:12,778
Will we not be seeing a kiss scene in this project either?

207
00:14:13,408 --> 00:14:16,048
There are rumours that there is a real reason behind it.

208
00:14:16,108 --> 00:14:19,648
I am sure you know that I am not into men.

209
00:14:20,388 --> 00:14:23,448
Honestly, my skills are too breathtaking to show publicly,

210
00:14:23,518 --> 00:14:25,058
so I think the broadcasting committee would censor it.

211
00:14:25,118 --> 00:14:26,118
Well,

212
00:14:31,858 --> 00:14:34,998
I can prove it to you privately as much as you want.

213
00:14:40,908 --> 00:14:43,208
I suppose differentiating yourself from other romance actors...

214
00:14:43,268 --> 00:14:44,508
is a good strategy.

215
00:14:46,138 --> 00:14:47,748
Assuming you are not deceiving your fans...

216
00:14:47,808 --> 00:14:49,348
for some other reason.

217
00:14:53,178 --> 00:14:54,718
Are you not going to ask our leading lady any questions?

218
00:14:54,788 --> 00:14:56,818
As for Na Ri...

219
00:15:02,588 --> 00:15:05,498
Right. How do you take care of your skin, Na Ri?

220
00:15:05,558 --> 00:15:06,858
Excuse me? I don't do anything special...

221
00:15:06,928 --> 00:15:09,298
To act while also promoting with your girl group,

222
00:15:09,368 --> 00:15:10,368
what is the secret to your figure?

223
00:15:10,438 --> 00:15:11,738
Do you have a special routine?

224
00:15:13,168 --> 00:15:15,568
I just eat well and move around a lot...

225
00:15:15,668 --> 00:15:16,668
I see.

226
00:15:19,108 --> 00:15:20,108
Actor Um,

227
00:15:20,178 --> 00:15:22,178
people say your acting range has broadened.

228
00:15:22,248 --> 00:15:24,318
What did you focus on the most while acting?

229
00:15:24,718 --> 00:15:25,718
My pores.

230
00:15:25,778 --> 00:15:27,688
(The Cocky Detective and Con Artist)

231
00:15:27,748 --> 00:15:30,218
Male actors care a lot about their skin too,

232
00:15:30,718 --> 00:15:32,488
since TV resolution is incredible these days.

233
00:15:33,118 --> 00:15:35,658
But this friend here is different from me.

234
00:15:35,988 --> 00:15:39,528
On set, Song Na Ri's nickname is "Tattered."

235
00:15:40,328 --> 00:15:42,698
How do you get your script so tattered?

236
00:15:43,968 --> 00:15:45,638
Well, it is not that bad.

237
00:15:46,038 --> 00:15:47,208
Oh, you should tell her about that too.

238
00:15:47,268 --> 00:15:49,408
You are learning boxing these days.

239
00:15:50,508 --> 00:15:52,738
You said you really want to use your fists,

240
00:15:53,108 --> 00:15:54,778
but don't just swing them anywhere.

241
00:15:58,148 --> 00:16:02,718
I am going to take a break first. My skin needs some moisturizing.

242
00:16:02,788 --> 00:16:03,788
Good work.

243
00:16:06,858 --> 00:16:08,028
What is up with him?

244
00:16:08,088 --> 00:16:09,428
They say he gets sensitive when he has a shoot.

245
00:16:16,428 --> 00:16:17,768
I'm just grabbing some water.

246
00:16:18,038 --> 00:16:19,038
Oh my.

247
00:16:21,108 --> 00:16:23,938
Through this project, what have you learned as an actress?

248
00:16:30,618 --> 00:16:32,178
Hey...

249
00:16:32,248 --> 00:16:34,148
- Thank you for earlier.
- For what?

250
00:16:35,088 --> 00:16:37,158
I was helping myself earlier, not you.

251
00:16:37,218 --> 00:16:38,218
The questions were so cliché...

252
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:39,918
that I was just looking for a time to escape.

253
00:16:39,988 --> 00:16:42,188
That kind of dullness is an enemy to the skin.

254
00:16:48,928 --> 00:16:50,738
Right.

255
00:16:50,798 --> 00:16:52,598
It is the truth.

256
00:16:52,668 --> 00:16:54,838
Your script being tattered.

257
00:16:54,908 --> 00:16:58,438
Keep making it tattered like that. But...

258
00:17:01,108 --> 00:17:04,748
don't ever let your heart get tattered.

259
00:17:15,828 --> 00:17:16,928
Gosh, it is cold.

260
00:17:19,258 --> 00:17:21,898
Hey, wasn't Tae Bong's acting amazing earlier?

261
00:17:21,968 --> 00:17:23,368
Pretending to take Song Na Ri's side...

262
00:17:23,428 --> 00:17:25,238
while putting the reporter in her place.

263
00:17:25,298 --> 00:17:27,838
